The release tooling (rel/, the GitHub workflows, the data-home rule, the
update check and the launcher's Details endpoint) and the join and link
clients came from Alnasl (https://github.com/teapot-chess/Alnasl) and
Arkab (https://github.com/teapot-chess/Arkab), by the same owner. Changes: the names (Alnasl/Arkab -> Nunki), the
port, what is kept (a JSON file instead of a database) and what is talked
about over the link.

The Windows release carries Microsoft's Visual C++ runtime DLLs
(vcruntime140.dll, vcruntime140_1.dll, msvcp140.dll) beside erl.exe, as
Microsoft allows for programs that need them.

Speech is produced by the operating system's own engines (Windows speech,
macOS say, espeak-ng or speech-dispatcher); none of them is included.
